\"text\": \"His impressive high school career, which included a state championship and multiple All-American honors, had college scouts and coaches salivating at the prospect of landing him.\"}, {\"id\": \"s6\", \"text\": \"In the end, it was Duke University that won the coveted recruit, and Winslow's decision to don the Blue Devils' iconic blue and white would prove to be a game-changer for both the program and the player.\"}, {\"id\": \"s7\", \"text\": \"As Winslow stepped onto the Cameron Indoor Stadium court for the first time, the expectations were palpable.\"}, {\"id\": \"s8\", \"text\": \"Coach Mike Krzyzewski, the winningest coach in college basketball history, had a reputation for getting the most out of his players, and Winslow was no exception.\"}, {\"id\": \"s9\", \"text\": \"From the opening tip, it was clear that the 6'6\\\" small forward was something special.\"}, {\"id\": \"s10\", \"text\": \"His athleticism, length, and defensive prowess were on full display, as he quickly established himself as one of the top freshmen in the country.\"}, {\"id\": \"s11\", \"text\": \"Winslow's impact on the Blue Devils was immediate and profound.\"}, {\"id\": \"s12\", \"text\": \"He started in all 39 games, averaging 12.6 points, 6.5 rebounds, and 2.1 assists per contest.\"}, {\"id\": \"s13\", \"text\": \"His defensive skills, honed from years of playing against top-level competition in high school, allowed him to guard multiple positions, earning him a spot on the ACC All-Defensive Team.\"}, {\"id\": \"s14\", \"text\": \"But it was his clutch performances in big games that truly showcased his mettle.\"}, {\"id\": \"s15\", \"text\": \"In a thrilling 73-65 win over rival North Carolina, Winslow poured in 13 points, grabbed 9 rebounds, and blocked 3 shots, cementing his status as a fan favorite in Durham.\"}, {\"id\": \"s16\", \"text\": \"As the season progressed, Winslow's accolades piled up.\"}, {\"id\": \"s17\", \"text\": \"He was named ACC Freshman of the Year, earning 75 of 77 possible votes from the conference's media members.\"}]}"
